* Methods

⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000001⟫ does not have classes.
However, you can define methods on types.

A method is a function with a special ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000002⟫receiver⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000003⟫ argument.

The receiver appears in its own argument list between the ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000004⟫func⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000005⟫ keyword and
the method name.

In this example, the ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000006⟫Abs⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000007⟫ method has a receiver of type ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000008⟫Vertex⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000009⟫ named ⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000010⟫v⟪GTI18N_8a62096b_000011⟫.

